Executive Summary
The private equity industry represents one of the largest and most urgent buyers of AI
implementation services in the world today. With over $15 trillion in global assets under
management, approximately 4,100 firms managing roughly 19,000 funds, and each of those
firms overseeing anywhere from a handful to hundreds of portfolio companies, the addressable
market for hands-on AI transformation work is enormous.
The critical insight: PE firms are not technology companies. They are financial engineers and
operational specialists who buy businesses, improve them over 5-7 years, and sell them at a
higher multiple. AI has become the third pillar of value creation alongside financial engineering
and operational excellence. But most PE firms lack the internal talent to actually deploy AI
across their portfolio companies. They are actively searching for external partners who can
move fast, deliver measurable results, and speak the language of EBITDA improvement rather
than technology buzzwords.
This plan outlines how Precision Data Strategies can position itself to capture work from this
market, starting with mid-market PE firms where the barriers to entry are lowest and the need is
most acute.
