1.2 The Economics That Drive Urgency
Understanding the financial pressures on PE firms explains why this is a now-or-never market:
• Management fees (2% of AUM): A $1B fund generates $20M/year in fees. These fees
fund operations, including the value creation teams and operating partners who would
hire you. The money is there.
• Carry (20% of profits): The real money for PE firms comes from increasing portfolio
company value. If AI can boost EBITDA by even 10-15% across a portfolio, that
translates to hundreds of millions in carry. This is the lever that makes them desperate
for AI help.
• Hold period pressure: PE firms hold companies for 5-7 years. Every month of delay on
AI implementation is a month of lost value creation before exit. Speed matters
enormously.
• LP expectations: Limited Partners (the institutions that invest in PE funds) are now
demanding AI strategies across portfolios. Firms without an AI story are at a fundraising
disadvantage.
• Exit multiples: Portfolio companies with demonstrated AI capabilities are commanding
premium exit multiples. Companies without AI strategies are seeing valuation discounts.
• Dry powder pressure: PE firms are sitting on record levels of undeployed capital. LPs
are pushing for efficient allocation. AI is the tool that helps deployed capital create more
value.
