5. Identify one proof-of-concept client: If any of your current or past clients happen to be
PE-backed, reach out to the PE firm and offer a case study presentation. Even if you do
not have a PE-backed client yet, package your best results in PE-friendly metrics (cost
reduction %, revenue lift, time saved).
4.2 Phase 2: Outreach (Weeks 5-12)
1. LinkedIn outreach campaign: Personalized connection requests to operating partners.
Not a pitch. A value-add message referencing their firm's portfolio and a relevant AI use
case. Follow up with the whitepaper. Aim for 20-30 new connections per week.
2. Cold email campaign (Smartlead): You already have the infrastructure for this. Build a
dedicated domain set for PE outreach (separate from the beach resort campaigns).
Different ICP, different messaging, different domains. Target operating partners and
portfolio company CEOs simultaneously.
3. Strategic referral outreach: Connect with 5-10 PE recruiting firms (ECA Partners,
Heidrick & Struggles). Offer to be a resource they can recommend when their newly
placed AI Operating Partners ask for vendor recommendations.
4. Conference attendance: Identify the next ACG event in LA. Register. Prepare 30-
second and 2-minute versions of the PE pitch. ACG events are smaller and more
accessible than SuperReturn.
5. Marketplace listings: Apply to Catalant and GLG as an independent AI consultant.
These platforms are specifically used by PE operating teams to find implementation
help.
4.3 Phase 3: Land and Expand (Weeks 12-24)
1. Close the first AI Readiness Assessment: This is the beachhead. Price it attractively if
needed ($10K-$15K) to get in the door. Over-deliver on the deliverable. The assessment
report becomes your internal sales tool at that firm.
2. Convert assessment to implementation: Use the assessment findings to justify a full
implementation sprint at one portfolio company. Deliver fast. Measure everything. PE
firms move on data, so your results need to be quantified.
3. Request the portfolio-wide introduction: Once you have proven results at one
portfolio company, ask the operating partner to introduce you to other companies in the
portfolio. This is where the math gets exciting. You are no longer selling one company at
a time.
4. Build the case study: Document the first engagement with PE-grade metrics. This case
study becomes the centerpiece of all future PE outreach.
4.4 Phase 4: Scale (Months 6-12)
1. Replicate across the first PE firm's portfolio: Deploy to 3-5 more portfolio companies
using the playbook developed in Phase 3.
2. Secure a second PE firm: Use the case study from Firm #1 to open doors at Firm #2.
Operating partners talk to each other. One success story creates referrals.
