6. Competitive Landscape and Positioning
You need to understand who else is playing in this space and where PDS can differentiate:
Tier 1 Consultancies (McKinsey, Bain, BCG, Deloitte, EY, PwC): These firms are already
deeply embedded with PE. They do strategy and roadmapping but generally do not do hands-
on implementation. Their assessments cost $200K-$500K and take 3-6 months. PDS
advantage: you are faster, cheaper, and you actually build the thing. Position yourself as the
implementation partner that executes on the strategy the big firms produce.
AI Startups and Point Solutions: Companies like Blueflame AI, Kira Systems, and various
SaaS tools. These are product companies, not service companies. They sell a tool. PDS
advantage: you provide end-to-end implementation, integration, and ongoing management. You
are the glue between the AI tools and the portfolio company's operations.
