9. The Bottom Line
This is not a pivot. This is an expansion into a market where the demand is urgent, the budgets
are enormous, and the competition at the implementation level is thin. PE firms have the money.
Their portfolio companies have the need. And the big consultancies are too slow and too
expensive for the hands-on work.
PDS already builds the exact things these portfolio companies need: voice agents that handle
customer calls, automation workflows that eliminate manual processes, CRM integrations that
improve sales performance. The only thing that needs to change is who you sell it to and how
you talk about it.
The math is simple: one mid-market PE firm with 20 portfolio companies represents more
revenue potential than 100 individual SMB clients. Two or three PE firm relationships and PDS
is a multi-million dollar business. Ten PE firm relationships and you are approaching the $100K
MRR target from an entirely different angle, one that compounds faster than any other channel.
The AI consultant you spoke with today pointed you to a $15 trillion market that is actively
looking for people like you. The question is not whether PDS belongs in this space. The
question is how fast you can get in front of the right people.